<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Lower Lorraine</h1><p class="st-meta">959 CE – 1190 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The northern half of old Lotharingia, a duchy over the Low Countries whose title was carried by Godfrey of Bouillon and survived in Brabant.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 959 Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruno-the-great">Bruno</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-cologne">Cologne</a> divided the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-lotharingia">Duchy of Lotharingia</a>, creating a separate duchy for the lands of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. The German kings appointed its dukes, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-duke-of-lower-lorraine">Carolingian Charles</a>, brother of the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a>, from 977 to 991.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Ducal power was always limited, since counts such as those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuven">Louvain</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-hainaut">Hainaut</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-namur">Namur</a>, Holland and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-limburg">Limburg</a> and the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/prince-bishopric-of-liege">Liège</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-utrecht">Utrecht</a> built their own principalities. The emperors used the office to reward loyal families: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-i-of-louvain">Godfrey the Bearded's</a> house held it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godfrey-of-bouillon">Godfrey of Bouillon</a> was duke before leading the First Crusade in 1096.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From 1106 the title was disputed between the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuven">Louvain</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-limburg">Limburg</a>. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-schwabisch-hall">Diet of Schwäbisch Hall</a> in 1190 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Henry VI</a> limited the duke's authority to his own lands, and the Louvain dukes thereafter ruled as dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Brabant</a>, keeping the title duke of Lothier.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-lower-lorraine.jpg" alt="Duchy of Lower Lorraine" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Bundesministerium für Landesverteidigung · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Austria_(1-1).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>959 CE – 1190 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles of Lower Lorraine, Godfrey of Bouillon, Godfrey I of Louvain</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French and Middle Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lower Lotharingia, Lothier</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1074&amp;focus=duchy-of-lower-lorraine" aria-label="Duchy of Lower Lorraine on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4819 416 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Lower Lorraine lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5139 672L5139 672M5139 672L5229 694M5139 672L5098 671"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0M5229 694h0M5098 671h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5139 672h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5139 672h0"/></svg></a>